WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.768
[music]

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:05.071
NARRATOR: Fentanyl was first
created in Belgium in 1960.

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:06.539
[music]

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:08.541
NARRATOR: It was designed
for use in surgery

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:12.212
and to treat the most
severe forms of pain.

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:14.781
Over time, American
pharmaceutical companies

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:18.852
found a profitable way to market
related opioid medications

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:20.653
outside hospital settings.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:23.056
Since I've been on
this new pain medication

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:24.591
I have not missed
one day of work,

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:26.426
and my boss really
appreciates it.

00:00:26.493 --> 00:00:28.561
NARRATOR: Prescription
surged, and patients

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:31.364
were reassured that the
risk of addiction was low.

00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:35.869
Less than 1% of patients
taking opioids actually

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:37.937
become addicted.

00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:39.439
NARRATOR: They were very wrong.

00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:43.143
As fatal overdoses skyrocketed,
doctors made prescription

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:45.512
opioids harder to get.

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:49.649
Addicts turned to heroin,
and the crisis got worse.

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:53.987
Then in 2015, fentanyl
emerged on the black market

00:00:54.053 --> 00:00:55.422
in a big way.

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:58.925
Potent, cheap, and readily
available on the streets

00:00:58.992 --> 00:01:00.860
without a prescription.

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:06.032
In the US, overdose rates
exploded to record highs.

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:08.435
But here in Mexico,
fentanyl became a boon

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:09.502
to the underworld economy.

